UPDATE companies SET description='Carey, a former law enforcement officer with 25 years of experience, also owns Atelier Home, while Osborn brings global manufacturing expertise as owner of Beyond Borders Furniture Co. Their combined backgrounds in operations and design shaped the company into a trade-focused platform connecting people, product, and purpose.

The company manufactures custom upholstery and pillows in the United States, offering more than 300 fabric options with standard lead times of four to six weeks. It also produces handcrafted hardwood furniture and curates a portfolio of complementary brands. Operations include a domestic plant overseen by a plant manager, a distribution center, and an Asia-Pacific supply chain managed by a dedicated team. Showrooms in major markets, notably High Point, North Carolina, provide year-round access for trade partners.

RW Collective sells exclusively to the trade, serving retailers, interior designers, and industry professionals through a wholesale program that features tiered pricing, flexible ordering, and dedicated support including swatch services and inventory updates.

The founders emphasize that their contrast—operational discipline paired with creative vision—drives a system that delivers battle-tested quality and value. The company states that its offerings are vetted in real-world retail and design settings, ensuring reliability for partners who depend on consistent execution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom upholstery manufacturing", "Custom pillow manufacturing", "Hardwood furniture manufacturing", "Custom finishes and fabrics", "Wholesale trade program", "Trade showroom operations", "Supply chain management (Asia Pacific)"], "industries": ["Retail furniture", "Interior design", "Wholesale trade", "Design professionals"], "materials": ["Fabrics (300+ options)", "Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4-6 weeks for custom upholstery", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["USA-made custom upholstery with 300+ fabric options and 4\u20136 week lead times", "Curated brand portfolio developed specifically for retail partners", "Wholesale program with tiered pricing and flexible ordering", "Dedicated trade support including swatches and real-time inventory updates", "Products battle-tested in retail and design environments"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Rockford, Alabama -> db", "Founders Michael Carey and Rebekah Osborn -> /about", "Michael Carey background: 25 years law enforcement, owner of Atelier Home -> /about", "Rebekah Osborn background: owner of Beyond Borders Furniture Co. -> /about", "Custom upholstery made in USA with 300+ fabrics and 4-6 week lead times -> /", "Handcrafted hardwoods -> /about", "Curated brand portfolio for retail partners -> /about", "Wholesale program for retailers, designers, industry professionals -> / and /about", "Tiered pricing, flexible ordering, dedicated support with swatches and inventory updates -> /", "Showrooms in major markets including High Point, NC -> /about", "Team includes plant manager, distribution center manager, supply chain manager Asia Pacific -> /about", "Products battle-tested in retail and design environments -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "USA-made custom upholstery with more than 300 fabrics and dependable 4 to 6 week lead times.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rw-collective' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Race Tech Race Cars and Components, Inc. operates from Burlington, North Carolina, where it has built custom race cars since 1988. The company was founded by Russ Farmer, a champion driver and builder who remains president and CEO. What began as a specialist in dragster construction has grown into a full-service race-car manufacturer serving competitors across multiple classes.

The shop produces complete dragsters, roadsters, and doorslammers, each designed in CAD and fabricated in-house. Capabilities include aluminum and sheet-metal fabrication, MIG/TIG welding, tube bending, and CNC plasma cutting on a 4-by-8-foot table that handles aluminum, steel, and stainless up to 1/4-inch thick. Race Tech also assembles AN braided-stainless hoses as an authorized Goodridge distributor and provides in-house powder coating, polishing, chroming, custom painting, and graphics. A parts division stocks accessories and hardware, including Grade 8 fasteners used throughout its builds.

Customers range from NHRA world champions and big-money bracket racers to local enthusiasts. Recent winners in Race Tech cars include Brian Weber at Famoso Raceway, TG Paschal at Piedmont, and Anthony Bertozzi at the NHRA Sportsman Nationals. The company also serves local racers with nitrous bottle refills and one-off fabrication projects such as fuel cells, carts, and structural components.

Design features such as optimized driveline angles, 4-link brackets tuned for instant-center location, a removable crossmember for transmission access, and a master cylinder mounted outside the driver compartment reflect that focus. The in-house finishing suite eliminates outsourcing delays, giving teams a single source from chassis to paint.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom chassis fabrication", "Custom body fabrication", "Aluminum and sheet metal fabrication", "CAD design (AutoCAD)", "MIG/TIG welding", "Tube bending", "CNC plasma cutting (4''x8'' table)", "AN hose assembly (push fit, crimp, swage)", "Powder coating", "Polishing", "Chroming", "Custom painting", "Custom graphics", "Nitrous bottle refilling", "Race car package assembly (dragsters, roadsters, doorslammers)", "Parts and accessories distribution"], "industries": ["Drag racing", "Bracket racing", "Sportsman racing", "Motorsports"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Stainless steel", "Grade 8 hardware"], "equipment": ["4''x8'' CNC plasma cutting table", "MIG/TIG welding equipment", "Tube bending equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["CAD-designed chassis with optimized driveline angles for consistent ETs", "Removable crossmember allows transmission removal out the bottom", "Master cylinder mounted outside driver compartment to keep fluid off floor", "In-house powder coating, polishing, chroming, and custom painting/graphics", "Authorized Goodridge distributor for AN hose assemblies (push-fit, crimp, swage)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 -> /about", "Headquarters Burlington, NC -> db", "Russ Farmer founder/CEO -> /about, /", "Custom dragsters, roadsters, doorslammers -> /about, /", "CAD design, CNC plasma cutting 4''x8'' -> /services", "AN hose assembly (Goodridge authorized) -> /services", "In-house powder coating, polishing, chroming, painting -> /about, /services", "Grade 8 hardware used -> /", "Nitrous refills $20 minimum -> /services", "Customer examples: Brian Weber, TG Paschal, Anthony Bertozzi -> /", "35 years experience mentioned -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1988, Race Tech Race Cars and Components has been a leading manufacturer of fine racing machines.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "$20 minimum (nitrous refills)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='race-tech-race-cars-and-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Radcliff Wire, Inc. is based in Bristol, Connecticut, a historic center of spring manufacturing in the eastern United States. The company began over six decades ago as a supplier of hard-to-find flat and shaped wire to spring makers, and word of its quality and reliability spread quickly.

Today Radcliff Wire produces flat, square, and custom-profiled wire in more than 60 metals and alloys. It manages the entire production chain in-house, from raw-material certification through drawing, shaping, and final inspection. The facility maintains a suite of testing equipment — including Rockwell and micro-hardness testers, tensile testers, laser micrometers, and optical comparators — to verify mechanical properties and dimensional accuracy on every order.

The company serves a diverse industrial base that includes aerospace, electronics, medical devices, automotive, and consumer-products manufacturers.

Radcliff Wire attributes its longevity to a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2015, a cross-trained workforce that averages 15 years of experience, and a compliance program that covers REACH, RoHS, conflict-minerals, and DFARS requirements. The firm was founded to fill a gap in the spring-wire market and continues to focus on delivering the exact wire specification a customer needs, when they need it.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','REACH compliance','RoHS compliance','Conflict Minerals compliance (SEC Rule)','DFARS compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom shaped wire manufacturing", "Flat wire production", "Square wire production", "Special profile wire drawing", "Material certification and traceability", "Mechanical testing (hardness, tensile, micro-hardness)", "Dimensional inspection (laser micrometer, optical comparator)", "Metallurgical sample preparation and analysis", "REACH/RoHS/DFARS compliance documentation"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Electronics", "Medical devices", "Automotive", "Consumer products", "Spring manufacturing"], "materials": ["Aluminum alloy", "Brass", "Copper", "Copper beryllium", "Hastelloy", "Inconel", "Nickel", "Stainless steel", "Steel", "Tin", "Tin zinc"], "equipment": ["3 standard Rockwell hardness testers", "3 tensile testers", "1 Knoop/Vickers micro-hardness tester", "1 Ames portable Rockwell hardness tester", "5 microscopes with magnification up to 40x", "2 laser micrometers", "2 optical comparators", "Metallurgical mounting & measuring (Digital Video Image Generator)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "In-house metallurgical testing (hardness, tensile, micro-hardness, dimensional)", "Average employee tenure of 15 years with structured cross-training", "REACH, RoHS, conflict-minerals, and DFARS compliance support", "Over 60 metals and alloys available for custom shapes"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bristol, Connecticut -> /about", "Founded over six decades ago -> /about", "Produces flat, square, special shaped wire in 60+ metals -> /about", "Industries served: aerospace, electronics, medical, automotive, consumer products -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /quality", "REACH compliance -> /quality", "RoHS compliance -> /quality", "Conflict Minerals compliance -> /quality", "DFARS compliance -> /quality", "Testing equipment: Rockwell hardness testers, tensile testers, micro-hardness tester, portable hardness tester, microscopes, laser micrometers, optical comparators, metallurgical mounting -> /quality", "Average employee experience 15 years -> /quality", "Cross-training program -> /quality", "Materials: Aluminum alloy, Brass, Copper, Copper beryllium, Hastelloy, Inconel, Nickel, Stainless steel, Steel, Tin, Tin zinc -> /quality", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /about", "Headquarters: Bristol, Connecticut -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Radcliff Wire, Inc. produces flat, square, and special shaped wire in over 60 different metals and alloys.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["DFARS compliant material sourcing", "REACH compliance", "RoHS compliance", "Conflict Minerals compliance"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radcliff-wire-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Radian Machining was founded in 1996 in Santa Clara, California. The company operates as a precision machine shop serving technology, industrial, and medical sectors.

The shop provides CNC milling, CNC turning, surface grinding, and EDM services, along with machined heatsink production and combined milling-lathe operations. With a team of 10 to 49 employees, Radian focuses on prototype and short-run production of precision components, delivering complex parts with tight tolerances and fine surface finishes.

Customers span technology, industrial, medical, aerospace, and automotive industries. The company describes its work as supporting businesses that require consistent quality and predictable results, from engineering prototypes to production parts for digital and industrial applications.

Radian emphasizes its ISO 9001 certification and ITAR registration as evidence of its quality management and regulatory compliance. The company cites decades of experience, a state-of-the-art facility, and the craftsmanship of its technicians as factors that differentiate its service, particularly in sectors where every element must be flawless.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC Milling", "CNC Turning", "Surface Grinding", "EDM (Electrical Discharge Machining)", "Machined Heatsinks", "Milling & Lathe Combined Operations", "Fabrication", "Assemblies"], "industries": ["Technology", "Industrial", "Medical", "Aerospace", "Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype and short-run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Santa Clara, CA -> db", "Employee count 10-49 -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "Capabilities: CNC milling, CNC turning, surface grinding, EDM, machined heatsinks, milling & lathe combined, fabrication, assemblies -> /", "Industries: technology, industrial, medical, aerospace, automotive -> db and /", "Volume: prototype and short-run production -> db", "Company type: contract manufacturer/job shop -> db and /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Radian Machining provides CNC milling and turning services, specializing in prototype and short-run production parts.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "10-49", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radian-machining' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The trio set out to build an employee‑owned firm focused on technology and operational relevance for the U.S. Army’s Space and Missile Defense Command. The company is now headquartered in Ruston, Louisiana, and remains 100 % employee‑owned.

Today Radiance delivers intelligence analysis, cyber operations, directed‑energy (HEL/HPM) systems, hypersonics development, space communications and ISR, AI/ML for sensor data, and modeling‑and‑simulation support. It also runs a manufacturing complex capable of prototyping, low‑rate initial production, and hardware/software reverse engineering. The firm employs over 500 people across corporate facilities in nine states and project offices in fourteen states and one foreign country; intelligence work accounts for roughly 40 % of revenue.

Primary customers include the U.S. Army SMDC, the Intelligence Community, INSCOM, SOCCOM, NASA, and other DoD agencies. Testimonials cite the Chief of the Army’s High Energy Laser Division, the 116th MI Brigade Commander, and INSCOM’s G3 AISR Division Director as references.

