UPDATE companies SET description='Ramco Solutions operates from Laurel, Delaware, where it emerged as the successor to Planned Poultry Renovations, a company Brian Ramey co‑founded in 1995 after a career that began at Perdue Farms in 1983 and continued as engineering manager at Townsend’s. The business remains family‑owned, with Ramey’s son Kolby and daughter Hali now involved in its direction.

The shop designs, fabricates, and installs food‑grade conveyance systems — packaging, meat, and cook‑plant conveyors — along with mezzanines, maintenance platforms, trench covers, and vacuum equipment. In‑house capabilities span 4 kW fiber‑laser cutting (up to 1 in. mild steel), 180‑ton press‑brake forming, 110‑ton ironworking, TIG/MIG/stick welding, 3D LIDAR scanning, Autodesk Inventor modeling, and additive manufacturing in polycarbonate, carbon‑fiber blends, and Ultem. A proprietary Ramcoat non‑slip coating is applied to stair treads, floor plates, and other metal surfaces.

Primary customers are poultry and food‑processing plants, as well as broader food‑and‑beverage manufacturers that need hygienic, modular material‑handling solutions. The company also supplies components to other builders of food‑grade machinery.

Ramco was created to bring plug‑and‑play conveyor designs, standardized parts, and a streamlined quoting process to an industry that often relies on custom‑one‑off engineering. Its stated mission emphasizes pioneering new equipment through R&D, while its safety program includes OSHA 30/10, Highwire, Avetta, and ISN certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['OSHA 30 (Superintendent)','OSHA 10 (All workforce)','Highwire Certified','Avetta Certified','ISN Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber laser cutting (up to 1\" mild steel, 0.75\" stainless/aluminum)", "Press brake forming (180 ton, 10 ft)", "Ironworking (110 ton Piranha)", "TIG, MIG, and stick welding", "3D LIDAR scanning", "3D CAD modeling with Autodesk Inventor", "Ramcoat non-slip coating application", "3D printing (polycarbonate, carbon fiber blend, Ultem)", "Turn-key project management (design, fabrication, installation, commissioning)", "Steel erection", "Millwright services (alignment, installation, maintenance)", "Sandblasting (10x20 ft booth, Schmidt recovery)", "Wet saw cutting (FMB Omega, 9.5\" capacity)", "Plate rolling (Faccin 4-roll, up to 0.25\" stainless)", "Oxy-fuel and plasma torch cutting", "Sheet metal nibbling", "2D/3D drafting and design", "Food & beverage plant consulting", "Mechanical engineering consulting", "Modular conveyor system fabrication"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Poultry processing", "Food and beverage manufacturing"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Mild steel", "Galvanized steel", "Aluminum", "Polycarbonate", "Carbon fiber blend plastics", "Ultem"], "equipment": ["Trulaser 4 kW fiber laser", "Trubend 3170 180-ton press brake (10 ft)", "Piranha 110-ton iron worker", "ShopBot CNC router", "10'' x 20'' sandblast booth with Schmidt blast recovery", "FMB Omega wet saw", "Faccin 4-roll 4HEL-2120 plate roll"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Plug\u2011and\u2011play modular conveyor models with standardized parts", "Proprietary Ramcoat slip\u2011resistant, sanitary metal coating", "In\u2011house 3D LIDAR scanning for precise as\u2011built digital twins", "Turn\u2011key project execution from design through commissioning", "Workforce certified to OSHA 30/10, Highwire, Avetta, and ISN"], "facts_used": ["Location: Laurel, DE -> db", "Founder Brian Ramey, career at Perdue (1983), Townsend''s, co-founded Planned Poultry Renovations (1995) -> /about-us", "Family-owned with son Kolby and daughter Hali -> /about-us", "Products: food-grade conveyors, mezzanines, platforms, trench covers, vacuum equipment -> /", "Processes: laser cutting, press brake, ironworking, welding, LIDAR scanning, 3D modeling, 3D printing, Ramcoat coating -> /services", "Equipment: Trulaser 4kW fiber laser, Trubend 3170 press brake, Piranha iron worker, ShopBot CNC router, sandblast booth, FMB Omega wet saw, Faccin plate roll -> /services", "Certifications: OSHA 30, OSHA 10, Highwire, Avetta, ISN -> /services", "Materials: stainless, mild steel, galvanized, aluminum, polycarbonate, carbon fiber blend, Ultem -> /services", "Industries: food processing, poultry, food & beverage -> /about-us, /services", "Mission/vision: plug-and-play modular conveyors, standardized parts, R&D -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ramco Solutions is a custom fabrication company that specializes in the design, fabrication, and installation of food grade machines and components.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/68221049/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ramco-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ramtel Corporation, based in Johnston, Rhode Island, was founded in 1983 as Ramtech following the divestiture of the telephone industry and a collaboration with an Ivy League university in New England. The company set out to solve the vandalism and durability problems of standard receiver phones by developing the first hands-free security phone.

Today Ramtel manufactures a range of security communication products including custom silk-screened phone panels, one-button and dual-purpose hands-free phones in standard and mini sizes, multi-button phones, elevator phones with stainless steel panels, and area-of-refuge phones. All products are assembled in the USA.

Its phones are compatible with more than 30 PBX and VoIP platforms—including Avaya, Cisco, Asterisk, and Siemens—and are deployed for emergency assistance, elevator communication, entrance security, and area-of-refuge applications.

The company emphasizes that it is the only U.S. manufacturer producing non-rusting stainless steel columns, and it differentiates itself through a fierce commitment to custom solutions, rapid introduction of new features, and end‑to‑end customer support from engineering through installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom silk screening", "Anodized aluminum panel fabrication", "Stainless steel column fabrication", "Conformal coating of electronics", "Weatherproof and vandal-resistant assembly", "Phone line powered circuit design", "Low voltage heater integration", "Surge and grounding protection", "Tamper-resistant hardware installation", "Condensation protection (back box)", "EEPROM nonvolatile memory programming", "Automatic gain offset calibration", "Programmable muted speaker configuration", "Password-protected remote programming", "ACA (All Campus Alert) compatibility", "Auto-redial and emergency override functions", "Auto-answer and area monitoring", "Voice and location identification signaling", "ADA-compliant indicator lights and Braille plaques", "Phone diagnostics with Reliance 12 software", "Automatic and remote shut-off", "Adjustable time-out functions", "External output control (strobe, door/gate release, camera control)"], "industries": ["Safety and security", "Education (K-12)", "Elevator and lift", "Campus security", "Area of refuge", "Commercial real estate", "Telecommunications/VoIP"], "materials": ["Anodized aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Chrome-plated metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1983 -> /about", "Located in Johnston, Rhode Island -> /about", "Formerly Ramtech -> /about", "Manufacturer of security communication products -> /about", "Custom silk screened phone panels -> /", "Hands-free emergency phones (standard and mini) -> /", "Elevator phones with stainless steel panels -> /", "Only company fabricating columns in non-ru