UPDATE companies SET description='Rebo Lighting and Electronics is headquartered in Sparta, Tennessee, with a major tech center in Plymouth, Michigan. The company''s roots trace back to automotive lighting bulb manufacturing; the Sparta plant was launched in 1972, and the business evolved through mergers including the combination of Wagner and Tung‑Sol to become a large-scale bulb producer. Today Rebo operates as a global development and supply partner for innovative automotive lighting systems, with additional manufacturing and technical sites in Eisenach, Germany; Chongqing, Shanghai, and Wuxi, China; and a planned Eastern Europe location.

The company designs, engineers, and manufactures exterior and interior lighting systems. Its in‑house capabilities span design, optical engineering, R&D, metallization, projection and holographics, prototyping, surface‑mount technology (SMT), high‑speed automation, injection molding, and plastic welding. Rebo''s manufacturing footprint includes dedicated production facilities in Sparta, Eisenach, Chongqing, and Wuxi, supported by tech centers in Plymouth, Eisenach, and Shanghai. The firm reports serving more than 40 global OEMs.

Rebo''s customer base consists almost entirely of automotive original equipment manufacturers. A noted example is the first lit badge produced for the Ford Mustang. The company positions itself as a flexible, knowledgeable partner for unique automotive lighting challenges, drawing on a history that includes shipping over five billion bulbs before exiting the bulb business.

Rebo emphasizes its over 100 years of accumulated experience and a commitment to innovative, reliable lighting solutions that balance safety, comfort, and style. The firm''s differentiation rests on its integrated design‑to‑manufacturing model, global footprint, and ability to deliver fast, flexible solutions for complex automotive lighting programs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design", "Technology", "Optics", "R&D", "Metallization", "Projection and Holographics", "Prototyping", "Surface-mount Technology (SMT)", "High Speed Automation", "Injection Molding", "Plastic Welding", "Fabrication"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Automotive lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SMT line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 100 years of automotive lighting experience", "Integrated design, prototyping, and manufacturing under one roof", "Global footprint with tech centers in the US, Germany, and China", "Serves 40+ global automotive OEMs", "In-house SMT, injection molding, and plastic welding capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Sparta, Tennessee -> db", "Sparta plant launched 1972 -> db (products array)", "Global development and supply partner for automotive lighting systems -> homepage", "Capabilities: Design, Technology, Optics, R&D, Metallization, Projection and Holographics, Prototyping, SMT, High Speed Automation, Injection Molding, Plastic Welding -> /capabilities", "Locations: Plymouth (MI), Sparta (TN), Eisenach (Germany), Chongqing (China), Shanghai (China), Wuxi (China) -> homepage", "Serves 40+ global OEMs -> homepage", "First lit badge product for Ford Mustang -> db (products array)", "Over 100 years of experience -> /capabilities", "Fast, Flexible, and Knowledgeable Solutions for Unique Automotive Challenges -> db (industries_served)", "Merge with Tung-Sol, Wagner merged with Tung-Sol -> db (industries_served)", "Company forms into Chongqing Yanfeng Johnson Controls Automotive Co