UPDATE companies SET description='Rebuilders Automotive Supply (RAS) operates from Coventry, Rhode Island, with a second location in Tampa, Florida. The company has been a global full-line buyer of automotive cores for more than 50 years, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not provided in available sources.

RAS purchases automotive cores from a network of over 2,000 salvage yards, metal recyclers, and self-service yards worldwide. The company provides an online inventory and valuation software platform, backed by patented technology, to help suppliers maximize core yield and profits. RAS positions itself as the largest supplier to the largest remanufacturers, offering a full-line core buying service supported by experienced purchasing professionals.

The primary customers are automotive remanufacturers who require a steady supply of cores for rebuilding. RAS also serves core suppliers, surplus dealers, salvage yards, and metal recyclers by providing a web-based purchasing network that connects them with buyers.

RAS differentiates itself through its patented valuation technology and online software, which aim to increase the yield on vehicles and prevent cores from being crushed. The company emphasizes its extensive global network and long-standing experience as key reasons suppliers and remanufacturers choose its services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Core purchasing", "Core valuation", "Online inventory management", "Patented yield optimization", "Global core supply network management"], "industries": ["Automotive remanufacturing", "Salvage yards", "Metal recycling", "Automotive core supply"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented core valuation technology", "Online inventory and valuation software for suppliers", "Global full-line core buyer with over 50 years of experience", "Largest supplier to the largest remanufacturers", "Network of over 2,000 salvage yards, metal recyclers, and self-service yards"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Coventry, RI and Tampa, FL -> /", "Global full-line buyer of cores for more than 50 years -> /", "Online inventory and valuation software with patented technology -> /", "Largest supplier to largest remanufacturers -> /", "Network of over 2000 salvage yards, metal recyclers, self-service yards -> /", "Company name Rebuilders Automotive Supply -> db", "Website coresupply.com -> db", "Industry partnerships focus -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "RAS has been a global full-line buyer of cores for more than 50 years.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rebuilders-automotive-supply-rhode-island' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Redefined Woodworking Co. operates from Menifee, California, where founders Eric and Sara Ruby established the business after their marriage in 2017. Eric, a U.S. Naval Academy graduate with a mechanical engineering degree, and Sara, a former teacher with a teaching credential from Cal Poly San Luis Obispo, turned Eric’s woodworking hobby into a venture while he continued his Navy service. The couple relocated twice with the military before settling in Southern California to build the company.

The workshop produces handcrafted, American-made furniture with a focus on custom dining tables, along with other bespoke pieces. Services include furniture design consulting, wood species education, material selection guidance, and woodworking classes for enthusiasts. Each project moves through an inquiry, consultation, and delivery phase, with the team handling assembly on-site. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

The company serves residential clients seeking heirloom-quality furniture tailored to their spaces, as well as hobbyists attending woodworking classes. Customers are typically families and homeowners who value durable, customizable pieces made from solid wood. The Rubys’ emphasis on the dining table as a gathering point shapes their primary market.

