UPDATE companies SET description='Remcon Plastics was founded in November 1982 by Peter and Doren Connors in Pennsylvania. The venture was backed by the savings of both families — Bill and Nancy Remmey (Doren’s parents) and Lorraine Connors (Pete’s mother) — and named Remcon in their honor. The founders bet that a small, family-owned rotational molding company could compete with larger manufacturers by building better products and standing behind them. In 1990, after eight years in Conshohocken, the company moved to Reading, Pennsylvania, tripling its plant size.

Today, Remcon operates a 75,000-square-foot facility in Reading with eight rotational molding machines. It produces material handling containers, MASH-compliant water-filled traffic barricades and longitudinal channelizers, and custom OEM rotationally molded components. Automation and advanced production systems enable output levels uncommon in rotational molding, supporting steady production and reliable deliveries. Key engineering innovations include the reinforced beaded ''R'' lip that eliminated a common bulk-bin failure point, and a replaceable pallet system that extends container life by separating the wear component from the structural body.

Remcon serves traffic safety, material handling, and custom OEM markets. Its traffic safety line includes MASH-compliant water-filled barricades and channelizers built for real-world jobsite performance. Material handling products range from bulk bins and hoppers to the FBP bin with an integrated pallet. The company also provides custom rotational molding for OEM customers; one of its first OEM accounts from the early 1980s remains a customer today. Products are sold through a network of regional representatives across the United States and territories.

The company’s differentiation rests on durability, disciplined engineering, and integrity. Founder Pete Connors, an engineer with an MBA, applied stress-crack-resistant polyethylene formulations from DuPont to re-engineer common failure modes, raising industry standards for bin longevity from 12–24 months to over 10 years. Remcon remains family-owned and actively led by the founder, with the next generation — Tracy Connors as Executive Vice President and CEO, and James Connors as Director of Design — bringing outside experience to modernize operations while preserving the original commitment to keeping their word.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotational molding", "Custom OEM rotational molding", "Material handling container manufacturing", "MASH-compliant traffic safety product manufacturing", "Product design and engineering (reinforced beaded rim, replaceable pallet system)", "Automation and advanced production systems", "Production scheduling and efficiency systems", "Production partner network for geographic reach"], "industries": ["Traffic Safety", "Material Handling", "Custom OEM"], "materials": ["Polyethylene resins", "Stress crack resistant polyethylene (DuPont formulations)"], "equipment": ["Eight rotational molding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reinforced beaded ''R'' lip eliminates common bulk-bin failure points", "Replaceable pallet system separates wear component from structural body", "MASH-compliant water-filled barricades and longitudinal channelizers for jobsite performance", "Advanced automation and production systems deliver output levels uncommon in rotational molding", "Multi-generational family leadership with engineering focus"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Peter and Doren Connors in Pennsylvania -> /about-us", "Family-owned, backed by Remmey and Connors families -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Reading, Pennsylvania since 1990 -> /about-us", "75,000 sq ft facility with eight rotational molding machines -> /about-us", "Produces material handling containers, MASH-compliant traffic safety products, custom OEM rotationally molded components -> /about-us", "Invented reinforced beaded ''R'' lip and replaceable pallet system -> /about-us", "MASH-compliant water-filled barricades and longitudinal channelizers -> /about-us", "Multi-generational leadership: Pete Connors (President), Tracy Connors (EVP/CEO), James Connors (Director of Design) -> /about-us", "One OEM customer from early 1980s still a customer -> /about-us", "Uses advanced production systems and automation -> /about-us", "Works with trusted production partners -> /about-us", "Pete Connors engineering degree and MBA, started in rotational molding 1977 -> /about-us", "Guardsafe 36 barricade introduced 2016 -> /about-us", "Product spotlights: Guardsafe 36, Dry Bulk Hopper, FBP bin -> /", "Traffic safety and material handling representative networks -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, the 75,000 square foot facility operates eight rotational molding machines and produces: Material handling containers, MASH-compliant traffic safety products, Custom OEM rotationally molded components", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='remcon-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rencher Industries operates from Winston-Salem, North Carolina. The business presents itself as a boutique manufacturer focused on the camera department of motion picture, broadcast, and new media productions.

The company designs and assembles all of its products in-house, with many components also fabricated internally. Its catalog includes power adapters such as the USB‑Sink 28V (a USB‑C PD 3.1 trigger delivering 28 V at 5 A), battery adapters for Arri SR cameras, the PowerBlock USB‑C PD Battery Adapter, the BreakerBatt, and voltage monitoring tools like the Micro Voltmeter and Inline Voltmeter. It also offers a Mini Production Router and custom‑machined brass T‑Studs.

Rencher serves the motion picture, broadcast, and new media industries, targeting camera departments and production crews. Concrete examples include the Arriflex SR Battery Adapter for Arri cinema cameras, the Intersex Plate for camera mounting, and the Mini Production Router for on‑set signal routing. The company also invites custom work, encouraging customers to request bespoke items.

