UPDATE companies SET description='Restoration & Performance Motorcars (RPM) is located in Vergennes, Vermont, in the Champlain Valley. The shop was founded in 1986 by Peter Markowski, who built the original red barn facility after a career in construction, banking, and heavy-truck sales. Markowski’s passion for classic European sports cars began in his teens when he acquired a Ferrari Barchetta and spent two decades restoring it to original condition. The business remained family-owned for nearly four decades until September 2024, when Markowski sold it to four longtime employees—Nate Barcomb, Rolf Humburg, Keith Carnevale, and Jennifer Valz—while staying on as part of the team.

RPM specializes in the restoration, maintenance, and sale of classic European sports cars, with a focus on Ferrari and Porsche models.

The company serves collectors and owners of classic European sports cars, particularly Ferrari and Porsche.

The business was born from Markowski’s personal dedication to preserving automotive history; his early experience restoring the Barchetta taught him the value of originality and the network of parts specialists. RPM emphasizes adherence to factory specifications and originality, a principle that continues under the new employee ownership.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Classic European sports car restoration", "Classic European sports car sales", "Classic European sports car maintenance", "Ferrari restoration and service", "Porsche restoration and service"], "industries": ["Classic European sports car restoration", "Specialty car sales", "Automotive service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in Ferrari and Porsche restoration and sales", "Employee-owned since 2024 with founder still involved", "Nearly four decades of operation in the Champlain Valley", "Focus on originality and factory-correct craftsmanship"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1986 by Peter Markowski -> /about", "Family-owned restoration shop in Vergennes, Vermont -> /about, /", "Specializes in Ferrari and Porsche -> /about, /", "Sold to employees Nate Barcomb, Rolf Humburg, Keith Carnevale, Jennifer Valz in September 2024 -> /about", "Located at 462 Monkton Road, Vergennes, VT 05491 -> /, /about", "Offers restoration, sales, maintenance, and service -> /", "Operates in Champlain Valley of Vermont -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "RPM is a family-owned restoration shop in Vergennes, Vermont that sells and services classic sports cars", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='restoration-performance-motorcars' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Restronics New England operates from Framingham, Massachusetts, serving the six-state New England region as a manufacturers'' representative firm. The company is led by Managing Partner Hunter Adams, who brings 35 years of industry experience, alongside Manufacturers'' Representative Scott O''Donnell. While the firm''s founding year is not publicly disclosed, it presents itself as a national manufacturers'' representative organization with a consultative approach to OEM sales representation.

The firm does not manufacture products but represents manufacturers of electronic manufacturing equipment and supplies. Its core services include ESD assessments, workstation ESD assessments, and assembly line consultations for surface-mount and through-hole processes. All consulting services are provided at no charge to customers, with the team traveling to client facilities throughout Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Connecticut, New Hampshire, Vermont, and Maine. Restronics also manages distribution channel relationships and provides end-customer activity reporting for its manufacturer partners.

