UPDATE companies SET description='Robco Steel Fabricators operates from Wells River, Vermont, where it was founded in 1985 by brothers Bill and Bob Rowden. The business grew out of Rowden’s Dairy, a multi-generational family dairy operation, when the brothers recognized a local need for construction and maintenance of feed mills. They rebranded the dairy as Robco Steel Fabricators, the name drawn from Rowden Bros. Corp.

The company provides steel and miscellaneous metal fabrication, structural steel fabrication and installation, CNC plasma cutting, handrail and stair systems, equipment and truck repair, custom attachments, and on-site welding and installation. Through sister companies Rowden Crane & Rigging and New England Millwrights, Robco also offers trucking, rigging, and millwright services, creating a single source for design, fabrication, and installation. The shop serves customers within a 100-mile radius of Wells River.

Robco works across residential, commercial, and industrial construction, with early roots in agricultural feed-mill projects.

