UPDATE companies SET description='SPF Electric, LLC operates from Angleton, Texas, on the Gulf Coast. The company does not publish a founding year, but its own materials cite over 25 years of immersion in the electrical power sector and nearly two decades of experience.

The shop specializes in electrical manufacturing and fabrication, offering bus fabrication (precision cutting, bending, punching, and shearing of copper and aluminum bus bar, plus aluminum bus bar welding), switchgear fabrication (CNC cutting, vertical and horizontal press brakes, iron worker, welding, and stud welding), G10/GP03 component machining (barriers, bus supports, circuit breaker operating rods), relay panels and switchgear doors, and powder coating. All services — design, drafting, fabrication, powder coating, gasket installation, and hardware assembly — are performed in-house, which the company says enables quicker turnarounds.

SPF Electric serves industrial, petrochemical, and electrical testing markets, with a noted focus on the Texas Gulf Coast area. Customers include maintenance and engineering departments needing replacement or custom doors, panels, covers, and structural components for switchgear, motor control centers (MCCs), and transformers.

The firm emphasizes that centralizing design, fabrication, and finishing under one roof reduces lead times and improves quality. It also promotes its reverse-engineering capability and extensive library of factory drawings for relays, lights, switches, latches, push buttons, and accessories as a way to solve challenges for modern maintenance and engineering teams.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bus fabrication (cutting, bending, punching, shearing copper/aluminum bus bar)", "Aluminum bus bar welding", "Switchgear fabrication", "CNC cutting", "Press brake forming (vertical and horizontal)", "Iron worker operations", "Welding and stud welding", "G10/GP03 machining (barriers, bus supports, operating rods)", "Relay panel and switchgear door fabrication", "Powder coating (primer, color coat, UV preventative)", "Gasket installation", "Hardware assembly", "Reverse engineering of electrical components", "CAD design and drafting"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Petrochemical", "Electrical testing", "Electrical power generation and distribution", "Maintenance and engineering services"], "materials": ["Copper", "Aluminum", "G10 / GP03 (glass epoxy laminate)"], "equipment": ["CNC cutting machines", "Vertical press brakes", "Horizontal press brakes", "Iron worker", "Welding equipment", "Stud welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Quote within 3\u20135 days; normal service 1\u20132 weeks or 4\u20136 weeks; rush service available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All services in-house (design, drafting, fabrication, powder coating, gasket installation, hardware assembly)", "Reverse engineering of doors, panels, covers for switchgear, MCCs, transformers", "Extensive library of factory drawings for electrical accessories", "Quick quote turnaround (3\u20135 days) and rush service option"], "facts_used": ["Location: Angleton, Texas -> db and pages ''/'' and ''/about''", "Over 25 years in electrical power sector -> page ''/about''", "Nearly 20 y