UPDATE companies SET description='STI Electronics, Inc. is headquartered in Madison, Alabama. The company was founded in 1982 by Jim D. Raby, P.E., in San Dimas, California, as a family-run business.

The firm provides electronic contract manufacturing, engineering services, analytical testing, and IPC-authorized training. Its manufacturing capabilities include PCB assembly (surface-mount and through-hole), rapid prototyping, new product introduction builds, design-for-manufacturing review, rework and repair, conformal coating and encapsulation, and both leaded and lead-free soldering.

STI serves customers in aerospace, defense, medical, industrial, and energy markets, focusing on safety-critical and military-grade applications where precision and reliability are paramount.

Raby’s background in developing NASA and Department of Defense soldering schools established a culture of technical rigor that remains central to STI’s differentiation. The company combines advanced manufacturing, analytical laboratories, and one of the industry’s most respected training programs under one roof to help customers reduce risk and solve complex manufacturing challenges.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract electronic assembly", "Rapid prototyping", "New Product Introduction (NPI) builds", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "PCB assembly (surface mount and through-hole)", "Rework and repair", "Advanced testing", "Fabrication note review", "Conformal coating and encapsulation", "Leaded and lead-free soldering", "Engineering and design services", "Failure analysis", "Materials testing", "Cleanroom manufacturing", "IPC-authorized training (J-STD-001, IPC/WHMA-A-620, IPC 7711/7721)", "NASA-STD-8739.4 crimp cable and harness training", "Custom training curriculum development"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Medical", "Industrial", "Energy"], "materials": ["Leaded solder alloys", "Lead-free solder alloys", "Conformal coating materials", "Encapsulation materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering-driven manufacturing for safety-critical and military-grade applications", "Integrated manufacturing, engineering, analytical labs, and IPC-authorized training", "Cleanroom production with in-house failure analysis and materials testing", "IPC Authorized Training Center offering courses in Alabama, Texas, and onsite", "Over four decades serving aerospace, defense, medical, industrial, and energy sectors"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1982 by Jim D. Raby -> /about-us", "Relocated to Madison, Alabama in 1993 -> /about-us", "Over fifty professionals -> /about-us", "ISO9001 and AS9100 certifications -> db", "IPC Authorized Training Center -> /", "Facilities in Madison, AL