UPDATE companies SET description='Salute Apparel is a veteran-owned custom apparel company based in Boise, Idaho. Founder Aaron Hale launched the business from his garage in 2015, then expanded by acquiring the long-standing Boise shop T‑shirts Plus in 2016. Further purchases of Bulldog Shirt Shop (2018), Two Ocean Prints (2020), Custom Image (2022), and Idaho Shirt Shack (2026) gave the company a second location in Nampa and a growing regional footprint.

The company provides screen printing with plastisol inks on cotton, cotton‑poly blends, and synthetic fabrics; embroidery for text, outlines, filled designs, and custom patches; in‑house graphic design that accepts .ai, .eps, and .pdf files; customized online storefronts that handle ordering, production, and shipping for schools, teams, and businesses; and a range of promotional products such as journals, pens, water bottles, and mugs. Operations run out of two Idaho facilities with a staff that includes screen‑print and embroidery technicians, designers, and sales personnel.

Salute Apparel serves educational institutions, sports leagues, clubs, nonprofit organizations, and corporate clients needing uniforms, spirit wear, and branded merchandise. The customized storefront service is aimed at groups that want a hands‑free way to manage recurring apparel orders, while the promotional‑product line supports marketing giveaways and employee gifts.

Hale has stated that the business was started to give the community tools for self‑expression, framing the need to create and tell one’s story as a basic human right. The veteran‑owned ethos and a focus on local acquisitions are presented as the foundation of the company’s approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing (plastisol inks)", "Embroidery", "Graphic design", "Customized online storefronts", "Promotional products sourcing"], "industries": ["Education", "Sports teams", "Clubs and organizations", "Corporate uniforms", "Promotional products"], "materials": ["100% cotton", "Cotton-polyester blends", "Synthetic fabrics", "Promotional product substrates (journals, pens, water bottles, mugs)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and operated", "Customized online storefronts for hands-free group ordering", "In-house screen printing and embroidery under one roof", "Graphic design support for print-ready files", "Series of local acquisitions expanding capacity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2015 by Aaron Hale -> /about", "Veteran-owned business -> /about", "Acquisitions: T-shirts Plus 2016, Bulldog Shirt Shop 2018, Two Ocean Prints 2020, Custom Image 2022, Idaho Shirt Shack 2026 -> /about", "Locations: Boise and Nampa, Idaho -> /about", "Services: Screen printing, embroidery, graphic design, customized storefronts, promotional products -> /services", "Screen printing on cotton, cotton-poly blends, synthetic fabrics -> /services", "Embroidery for text, outlines, filled images, patches -> /services", "Graphic design accepts .ai, .eps, .pdf -> /services", "Customized storefronts for schools, sports teams, clubs, organizations, business uniforms -> /services", "Promotional products: journals, pens, water bottles, mugs -> /services", "Team members: Aaron, Candra, Cyndi, Kristi, Jason, Daisy, Kim, Rich -> /about", "Mission: give community tools to tell their stories -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We can print shirts with your existing design or help you create something new.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='salute-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sandbox VT operates from the south end of Burlington, Vermont, where it functions as a repair and circular services partner for clothing and gear. The company describes itself as a no‑bounds creators space promoting sustainable action through creativity and community. No founding year or founder names are publicly disclosed, and ownership structure has not been specified.

The shop provides expert repair, restoration, and alteration services for individuals, including clothing repair, technical outerwear and gear repair, backpack repair, zipper replacement, and mail‑in options. For business clients it runs warranty and repair programs, offers overflow repair capacity, technical sewing, product restoration, waterproofing, returns refurbishment, and small‑batch production that upcycles brand sample fabric into unique product runs. A curated selection of gently pre‑loved apparel is also sold monthly.

Customers range from individual consumers to outdoor brands, retailers, and designers who prioritize durability and circularity. The company cites work with outdoor brands and retailers needing warranty support, as well as designers seeking small‑batch upcycled collections. Bridal and formalwear alterations represent an additional service line.

